WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
In a disaster, people don't think like calculators, so we gave our agents a quantum mind.

00:03.000 --> 00:06.000
Volcano evacuation, quantum mind. Every cue nudges a quantum belief.

00:06.000 --> 00:09.000
Eruption! A certain cue collapses the belief.

00:09.000 --> 00:11.500
7 actions, 1 circuit. Stress drives decoherence.

00:11.500 --> 00:16.000
Same two cues, swapped order. Tremor then gas plume: P(danger) 0.459. Gas plume then tremor: 0.279.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.000
RMS Titanic, 1912. 2,208 people, one mind. Lifeboats at reconstructed launch times.

00:19.000 --> 00:22.000
Waterloo, Ontario. A real map, a chlorine leak.

00:22.000 --> 00:26.500
It hesitates like people do. Measurably. +0.55 steps later to evacuate than a matched classical agent. A model, not a prediction.

00:26.500 --> 00:30.000
Qognition. Quantum minds vs classical minds. Open source. Build your own worlds. Python and Qiskit.
